Connector/FPU configuration and original-unit preflight, 2026-09-28
==================================================================

This is NOT a kernel build, module installation, or runtime PASS. The currently
running paired tests retain their original Images, configuration and modules.

The existing source-pinned prerequisite audit verifies both reviewed source
contracts before and after solving the candidate with GCC14 olddefconfig.
Exactly three effective values change; no other enabled/disabled value changes:
  CONFIG_CONNECTOR    n -> y
  CONFIG_PROC_EVENTS  n -> y
  CONFIG_TEST_FPU     n -> m
ARCH_HAS_KERNEL_FPU_SUPPORT=y and KCOV_INSTRUMENT_ALL=n already hold.

An isolated output reuses the original read-only Linux source. Kbuild generates
the real headers and commands for five newly enabled original target-C units:
  drivers/connector/connector.o
  drivers/connector/cn_queue.o
  drivers/connector/cn_proc.o
  lib/test_fpu_glue.o
  lib/test_fpu_impl.o
All five compile and assemble with the current pinned Rust 1.97.1 EvoCC release;
all five match the GCC reference's externally defined symbols and symbol kinds.
No assembly is resumed from cache. The FPU implementation command removes
-mgeneral-regs-only and retains -ffreestanding and _LINUX_FPU_COMPILATION_UNIT;
the glue command retains -mgeneral-regs-only. No object is installed into the
active kernel. Existing K1 command projection and all omitted flags are recorded
in config-units.json; this does not newly establish diagnostic-option parity.

The resulting config still needs one uniform complete reference/subject build,
generated-input convergence, module signing/installation and unchanged connector
and FPU original execution on both matching Images. K12e/K12f remain OPEN.

